---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { receipt, timeline, syntheticCases } from '../showcases/session-cron/content';
const live = receipt.live_cli;
---
<section class="session-cron-showcase wrap" id="session-cron" aria-labelledby="session-cron-title" data-session-cron>
  <div class="cron-intro">
    <div><p class="cron-eyebrow">A schedule across two processes</p><h2 id="session-cron-title">The process stops.<br /><em>The schedule returns.</em></h2></div>
    <p>Claude Code supplies the native schedule. I built the engine-side checks and session bookkeeping around it. This recorded run resumes the same session in a new CLI process and receives the scheduled response without another prompt.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cron-record-label"><span>Recorded CLI test</span><span>15 October 2026</span><span>One non-recurring session cron</span></div>
  <ol class="cron-timeline" aria-label="Four recorded steps">
    {timeline.map((step, index) => <li><span class="cron-step-number">0{index + 1}</span><div><p class="cron-process">{step.process}</p><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.description}</p></div></li>)}
  </ol>
  <div class="cron-result" aria-label="Recorded result">
    <div class="cron-zero"><strong>{live.explicit_queries_after_resume}</strong><span>explicit queries<br /> after resume</span></div>
    <div class="cron-match"><p><Icon name="check" /><strong>{live.fixed_response_matched ? 'Fixed response matched' : 'Response did not match'}</strong></p><span>The saved result records the match. Prompt and response text are omitted.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="cron-observation">One observed answer arrived <strong>+{live.result_offset_from_mirror_seconds.toFixed(2)} seconds</strong> from the engine mirror’s predicted fire time. This is one recorded check, not a benchmark or timing guarantee.</p>
  <p class="cron-boundary">This check covers CLI session restoration and one scheduled answer. Engine restart, delivery callbacks and production health were outside the test.</p>
  <details class="cron-details" data-cron-synthetic>
    <summary>What comes back? Three saved classifier cases <Icon name="plus" /></summary>
    <div><p>These are <strong>fixed synthetic transcripts</strong> processed by the unchanged engine classifier. They are separate from the real CLI test above.</p>
      <table><caption>Selected results from 16 synthetic classifier cases</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Saved situation</th><th scope="col">Classifier result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{syntheticCases.map(row => <tr><th scope="row">{row.situation}</th><td><span class:list={['cron-case-result', { 'cron-eligible': row.restorable }]}>{row.result}</span></td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
      <p>A missed one-shot is dropped; this mirror does not promise catch-up. The seven-day recurring limit is its default. These examples do not establish every scheduling boundary in the native CLI.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <details class="cron-details" data-cron-evidence>
    <summary>What was recorded and checked <Icon name="plus" /></summary>
    <div>
      <p>The actual SDK and CLI ran in an isolated test. One explicit arming query created one non-durable, non-recurring cron. After that CLI closed, a different CLI resumed the same session with no query and no available tools. “Process A” and “Process B” distinguish those recorded processes; actual identifiers are omitted.</p>
      <p>The timeline is a projection of recorded events, not a chat recreation or a live scheduler. The fixed-response match is a comparison of the actual saved result; its raw text is omitted.</p>
      <div class="cron-evidence-counts"><p><strong>{live.sdk_product_interactions} SDK product interactions</strong><span>Initial arming and autonomous answer. SDK-reported <code>num_turns</code> was {live.sdk_num_turns.arming} and {live.sdk_num_turns.autonomous}; these are not provider inference or billing counts.</span></p><p><strong>{receipt.original_source_tests.unique_passed} unique original tests passed</strong><span>25 classifier tests and 24 mocked component tests. Separate from the 16 synthetic cases and this live CLI proof.</span></p></div>
      <p>My engine mirrors schedule eligibility from transcripts, restores the pinned session state and coordinates warming the session without a new prompt. The component tests isolate those responsibilities with mocked SDK, Redis and HTTP services.</p>
      <p>No real Claude Engine restart, armed-session record, Redis outbox, PanelForge callback or HTTP warm route was exercised. The current CLI’s full expression, timezone and expiry behavior was not verified by this one-shot run.</p>
      <p class="cron-versions">Engine source <code>{receipt.source.tag}</code> · SDK <code>{receipt.source.sdk_version}</code> · CLI <code>{receipt.source.cli_version}</code>. The mirror’s source comment references CLI 2.1.287; this recorded one-shot used 2.1.292.</p>
      <a href="/media/session-cron/receipt.json">Read the concise source receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
<style>
.session-cron-showcase{padding-block:42px 48px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:28px}.cron-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:24px 54px;align-items:end;margin-bottom:24px}.cron-eyebrow{color:var(--rust);font-size:13px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:12px}.cron-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.1rem,3.6vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.12}.cron-intro h2 em{color:var(--forest)}.cron-intro>p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);max-width:470px}.cron-record-label{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px 20px;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.cron-record-label>span:first-child{font-weight:650;color:var(--forest)}.cron-timeline{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));list-style:none;padding:0;margin:10px 0 24px;border:1px solid #aeb9a6;border-radius:4px;background:#faf9f2}.cron-timeline li{padding:20px 22px 24px;min-width:0;border-right:1px solid #c5cdbb}.cron-timeline li:last-child{border-right:0}.cron-step-number{display:block;color:var(--rust);font:italic 24px/1.2 var(--serif);margin-bottom:18px}.cron-process{font-size:12px;color:var(--forest);line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:8px}.cron-timeline h3{font-size:18px;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin-bottom:10px}.cron-timeline li>div>p:last-child{font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted)}.cron-result{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;background:#e6ecdc;border:1px solid #b3bfa7;border-radius:4px;align-items:center;gap:24px;padding:20px 26px}.cron-zero{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px}.cron-zero>strong{font:500 54px/1 var(--serif);color:var(--forest-dark)}.cron-zero>span{font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;font-weight:550}.cron-match>p{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;color:var(--forest-dark);font-size:16px;margin-bottom:4px}.cron-match>span{display:block;font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;color:#465443;max-width:470px}.cron-observation{font-size:13px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);padding:14px 0 0;max-width:910px}.cron-observation strong{font-weight:550;color:var(--forest-dark)}.cron-boundary{font-size:13px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);max-width:920px;margin:10px 0 22px}.cron-details{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.cron-details:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.cron-details>summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;min-height:54px;padding:14px 4px;font-size:14px;font-weight:550;cursor:pointer;list-style:none}.cron-details>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.cron-details[open]>summary :global(.ui-icon){transform:rotate(45deg)}.cron-details>div{padding:0 4px 24px;max-width:100%;min-width:0}.cron-details p{max-width:960px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:14px}.cron-details table{width:100%;max-width:850px;border-collapse:collapse;margin:18px 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65}.cron-details caption{text-align:left;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);padding-bottom:12px}.cron-details th,.cron-details td{text-align:left;padding:12px 16px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}.cron-details th{font-weight:550}.cron-details thead th{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.cron-details tbody th{width:62%}.cron-case-result{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.cron-eligible{color:var(--forest-dark);font-weight:650}.cron-evidence-counts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px 34px;padding:16px 0 4px;border-block:1px solid var(--line);margin-bottom:16px}.cron-evidence-counts strong,.cron-evidence-counts span{display:block}.cron-evidence-counts strong{color:var(--forest-dark);font-size:15px;font-weight:650;margin-bottom:5px}.cron-versions code{font-size:12px}.cron-details a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;font-size:14px;min-height:46px}.session-cron-showcase :global(.ui-icon){width:18px;height:18px;flex-shrink:0}
@media(max-width:1000px){.cron-intro{gap:24px}.cron-timeline li{padding:18px 16px}.cron-timeline h3{font-size:17px}.cron-result{grid-template-columns:.85fr 1.15fr;padding:20px}.cron-zero{gap:16px}}
@media(max-width:700px){.session-cron-showcase{padding-block:30px 36px}.cron-intro{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px;margin-bottom:20px}.cron-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,7.5vw,3rem)}.cron-intro>p{font-size:16px}.cron-record-label{font-size:12px;gap:4px 14px}.cron-record-label>span:last-child{flex-basis:100%}.cron-timeline{grid-template-columns:1fr;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:18px}.cron-timeline li{display:flex;gap:16px;padding:16px 18px;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid #c5cdbb}.cron-timeline li:last-child{border-bottom:0}.cron-step-number{margin:0;flex:0 0 28px;font-size:22px}.cron-process{font-size:11px;margin-bottom:4px}.cron-timeline h3{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:6px}.cron-timeline li>div>p:last-child{font-size:13px;line-height:1.65}.cron-result{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px;padding:18px}.cron-zero>strong{font-size:44px}.cron-zero>span br{display:none}.cron-zero>span{font-size:14px}.cron-match{border-top:1px solid #b3bfa7;padding-top:14px}.cron-match>p{font-size:15px}.cron-match>span{font-size:12px}.cron-details>summary{font-size:13px;min-height:54px}.cron-details th,.cron-details td{padding:12px 4px}.cron-details tbody th{width:60%;padding-right:14px}.cron-details table{font-size:13px}.cron-case-result{font-size:12px}.cron-evidence-counts{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0}.cron-evidence-counts>p:last-child{margin-bottom:12px}}
</style>
